# Kanban Workflow

**Canonical rule**: `../../.claude/rules/kanban-workflow.md` — full column ownership, SLAs, and transition rules.

**Board config**: `.claude/board-config.yml` in the project workspace root — contains `project_id`, `status_field_id`, and option UUIDs for the project's board.

## Summary

12-column pipeline: Backlog → FRD Draft → FRD Tech Plan → Tech Plan Approved → AI Development → Code Review → Staging Ready → Staging Review → Rework → Ready for Production → Done (+ Hotfix lane).

## AI autonomy depends on operating mode

Read the project's `.claude/stack-*.yml` `framework.mode` field (source of truth) and the `solo-vs-team-mode` rule.

- **Solo mode**: AI may **self-promote tickets** through every column except ✅ Done. Log each autonomous move as a ticket comment.
- **Team mode**: AI only moves tickets **out of** AI-active columns. Waits for humans to move tickets **into** AI-active columns.

Comment shape for any AI-initiated move:

```
Moved to <column> under <mode> mode on <YYYY-MM-DD>.
```

## AI-active columns (work happens here)

`🤖 FRD Tech Plan`, `💻 AI Development`, `🧪 Staging Ready`, `🔄 Rework`, `🚨 Hotfix`.

## How to move a ticket

```bash
# 1. Get item ID
gh project item-list <project_number> --owner <org> --format json

# 2. Move ticket (IDs from .claude/board-config.yml)
gh project item-edit \
  --project-id <project_id> \
  --id <item_id> \
  --field-id <status_field_id> \
  --single-select-option-id <status_option_id>
```

## Hard rules (apply in every mode)

- **Verification Gate** must pass before moving out of any AI-active column — pasted command output on the ticket.
- **Never merge to `master` / `main` / `dev`** — only to release branches (e.g. `release/ai-sdlc-v1`).
- **✅ Done is human-only** — AI never moves a ticket to Done, regardless of mode.
- **Hard stops** (destructive ops, financial, auth/permissions/secrets) still require chat confirmation.
